Z||000004||Formula88||07-08-2001||09:28 PM||||Beautiful!  Can't wait to hear how she runs!  LMK how you like the suspension setup.  Still stock springs?  Are you using the standard or HD KYB's up front?  <P>Awesome work!||||reg||14
Z||000005||88formula||07-08-2001||10:12 PM||||Thanks,<P>Formula88 the springs are stock. I have not driven the car yet with the new suspension setup. I still need to add the coolant and oil, prime the oiling system, and fix the master or slave cylinder that has failed because it sat for a year. The KYB shocks and struts are the softer GR-2 type. I liked the way the car handled and road stock so I built the suspension with ride comfort in mind. In New England potholes and rough roads are common. Driving in a low stiff riding fiero would be torture. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-08-2001).]||||reg||1
