Z||000013||StuGood||07-10-2001||01:09 PM||||Very sharp engine!  Nice job  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The working outside on grass pics remind me of when I replaced a lower control arm along with engine and transmission mounts on my Monza.  On the dirt in my back yard.  Not one of my more brilliant moves.  No fun, especially after it rained  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">.<P>The critter camping by the computer reminds me of when I used to always be clearing acorns out of the battery box in my Corvair. Finally one day I saw a chipmonk jumping up into the fender, then back down to the ground, back up into the fender, etc.  What's he doing-?<P>I had widened out the battery box in the fender, to accept a standard-size battery.  Part of the outer side of the box was open to the underside of the fender, and Mr. Chipmonk must have decided it made a great storage bin.<P>I must be getting to be an old guy - just about everything reminds me of a story or three  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">      ||||reg||10
Z||000014||88formula||07-10-2001||04:49 PM||||I built the engine myself. The block came from a 95 Camaro 3.4-liter engine. ||||reg||1
